  "body": "## Current candidate\n**Head `6ecd8023615a6e0b2dc269379fb059c656b38b6f`, tree `4c51962e030e9ea39c6498224c99eb40fbdd2f35`. Its own CI is pending.**\n\nThis integrates #821 at `e0c1ac3c` and #822 at `ff456fd8` while preserving the independently advanced source baseline `20eace37`.\n\n## Changes\n- Bounded v16 combines all 25 unsigned checked-cast pairs and bool eq/ne with declared effects and callee-effect propagation. Capacity limits and compiler symbols are unchanged.\n- Safe Core unsigned casts require an explicit v2 profile; v1 remains the default. Scoped assumptions and unproved obligations remain explicit.\n- The scalar stop guard is opt-in, preserves state/resource/cost/ledger checks, and never labels a skipped evaluation as native NDU execution.\n- Source CI retains the original frozen-compiler lifecycle and the separate current checked-in compiler lifecycle. Reports/logs remain; ephemeral state databases and sidecars are excluded.\n- The elapsed fixture anchors its accelerated interval at the collector's first clock read. Original elapsed/checkpoint subcases, child identity, cleanup assertions and process/cleanup budgets remain. An entry-delay case and three clock traces add no unique test-method IDs.\n\n## Integration identity\nIntermediate `50262236d9d1807ca8df0eccfb9f5f7ee9f6206c` has parents e0 and ff. The current candidate has ordered parents `20eace37747fde9aa0fc9c14cdb0159db30f5161` and that intermediate merge. Public source 2598 is already an ancestor.\n\nOrdinary local merges, including the baseline-first order, had no content conflicts. Eleven existing e0/ancestor blobs applied to the ff tree reproduce the exact final tree; both remote commits' trees and parents were independently read back. Relative to 6a there are 64 changed paths, no base deletions, all 380 prior evidence blobs retained and 25 added evidence paths. Only this PR's branch was advanced; the two source baseline refs remain unchanged pending qualification.\n\n## Validation and remaining gates\nPrevious head `6a8c297b` completed **19/19 workflows on attempt 1**, including initialization **80/80 jobs**. Its full cohort contains 113 successful jobs and one unrequested workflow_dispatch-only optional job; the separate native NDU integration passed. The two default-checkout jobs used the actual d8 merge with the same tree. The complete records, original failures and original source/NDU artifacts are retained in #823.\n\nThose results do not qualify this new head. Local v15 native records likewise bind their original e6-equivalent tree, not later fixture changes or this merged v16 candidate. Incomplete historical SIGKILL records remain marked incomplete. This candidate needs its own applicable CI and original source-CI lock before integration or promotion.\n\nThe public default remains verified v9. No live service change is part of this PR. Full Core selfhosting, general compiler/ABI/resources/FFI/ISA/loader correctness, the original unfamiliar-Agent four-claim gate and complete provider costs, and stable NDU incremental/economic value remain open. Scoped nonproduction lifecycle and fragment proofs do not close those broader obligations. **Overall six-track acceptance remains HOLD.**\n",
